# Enterprise Tasks Workspace — Platform Constitution

Status: **ENTERPRISE APPROVED** · Canonical Tasks + Planner desk  
Sprint foundation: **CO-TASKS-PLANNER-001** · UX: **CO-TASKS-PLANNER-001A** · Density: **CO-TASKS-PLANNER-002** · Workspace: **CO-TASKS-PLANNER-003**

## Constitutional principles

1. **One left-nav item:** Tasks (`/tasks`). Never add a separate Planner nav item.
2. **ETE is the only task engine.** Planner does not invent a parallel task store.
3. **Planner is a projection of the Enterprise Task Registry only** — Agenda / Day / Week / Month are calendar presentations of ETE tasks with due dates. Do not merge parallel Meeting/Reminder task stores into Planner events.
4. UI consumes **DTOs only** — compose in `src/lib/enterprise-tasks-workspace` and `src/lib/enterprise-planner`.
5. **Drag-and-drop reschedule** updates ETE `dueOn` + audit + dialogue timeline — never duplicates records.
6. **Shared schedule colour system** (Completed · Scheduled · Due Today · Due Tomorrow · Overdue · Cancelled) across Tasks and Planner.
7. External calendar sync (Google / Outlook) is **reserved** — do not implement until authorised.
8. **Agenda section order:** Today → Tomorrow → This Week → Overdue → Upcoming.
9. **Calendar-first density (002):** compact header · CHANAKYA LIVE single-strip ticker · metrics as lightweight toolbar · maximise Planner calendar height.
10. **Actionable workspace (003):** date-cell create intents · activity context menu · day overflow panel · Search / Filter / My–Team scope — all write through ETE.

## Primary tabs

| Tab | Role |
|-----|------|
| **Tasks** (default) | Execution — buckets, CRUD, bulk actions |
| **Planner** | Operational scheduling — Agenda / Day / Week / Month |

Deep-link: `?tab=planner` · `?view=agenda|day|week|month`

